{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/expanded-support-for-residents-living-with-unsafe-cladding","content_id":"2b61f398-058d-4d7e-8f57-8a793d6a2001","description":"Dangerous cladding will be removed from lower-rise buildings with serious fire safety risks, thanks to new government funding.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>The new funding for under 11 metre buildings will be part of the existing Cladding Safety Scheme, with support prioritised for those facing the greatest risk. </p>\n\n<p>Serious cladding problems are less common in lower-rise buildings, and they are not covered by existing leaseholder protections. As a result, leaseholders can be left facing large bills to fix safety issues they did not cause.</p>\n\n<p>The new funding will help protect leaseholders from these costs and ensure the most unsafe buildings can be made safe.</p>\n\n<p>It is part of a wider change to how buildings are prioritised for remediation. Instead of focusing mainly on building height, the government will prioritise buildings based on the risk they pose to residents, ensuring those with the most serious safety concerns are addressed first.</p>\n\n<p>Today’s announcement delivers on commitments set out in the Remediation Acceleration Plan and builds on work to address the failings set out in the Grenfell Inquiry. The upcoming Remediation Bill will go even further to ensure landlords deliver on their responsibility to fix unsafe buildings. </p>\n\n<h3 id=\"building-safety-minister-samantha-dixon-said\">Building Safety Minister, Samantha Dixon said: </h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>Residents shouldn’t be left worrying about living in homes with dangerous, flammable cladding, just because their building isn’t tall enough to qualify for funding.   </p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">That’s why we’re taking action so that buildings posing the greatest risk to life are prioritised, as well as streamlining processes to minimise delays and make responsibilities clear.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>To further support leaseholders, the government has welcomed a new review by the Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) into how insurance premiums for buildings with fire safety risks have changed since the FCA brought in new rules in 2023.</p>\n\n<p>The review will look at how insurers’ pricing approaches have changed over time, how firms are considering leaseholders’ interests when assessing whether their products deliver fair value, and how building remediation work is being taken into account in insurers’ risk assessments.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"economic-secretary-to-the-treasury-rachel-blake-said\">Economic Secretary to the Treasury, Rachel Blake said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>Too many leaseholders have spent years facing uncertainty and have been unable to move on with their lives because of building safety issues they did not cause.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">As we work to make buildings safer, leaseholders deserve confidence that they are paying a fair price for insurance. The FCA’s review will help us better understand how insurers are pricing and whether leaseholders are getting fair value.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>It supports wider efforts to make sure building safety issues are fixed quickly and fairly, without leaving leaseholders facing unreasonable costs. </p>\n\n<p>Following discussions with industry and resident groups, the government has also confirmed a range of changes to improve building safety regulation while reducing unnecessary delays. The changes include: </p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Setting out the government’s plans for a new Single Construction Regulator, which will bring together different parts of the building regulation system and make it easier to navigate. </li>\n  <li>Making it simpler for the Building Safety Regulator to issue Building Assessment Certificates and providing clearer guidance for building owners. </li>\n  <li>Launching a new consultation to make it easier for emergency works to take place, and publishing two consultation responses on telecommunications work and ensuring existing buildings can move through the regulatory process more swiftly, while maintaining safety standards.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Together, these changes will help keep residents safe while reducing unnecessary bureaucracy that can slow down essential building safety work. </p>\n\n<h3 id=\"chief-executive-of-the-national-housing-federation-kate-henderson-said\">Chief Executive of the National Housing Federation, Kate Henderson said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>We welcome the government’s decision to prioritise building safety remediation according to risk and to extend funding to lower-rise buildings with the most serious safety concerns. This is an approach the sector has long called for, as height alone is not a reliable measure of risk, and will ensure capacity is directed to where it’s needed most.</p>\n\n  <p>Housing associations continue to work hard to make all their buildings safe. The social housing sector is leading the way on remediation, but the scale and complexity of the challenge mean government support remains essential.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">This announcement is an important step towards accelerating remediation and ensuring residents in buildings of all heights feel safe in their homes. We will continue to work closely with the government to ensure all buildings with serious external wall safety risks are remediated as quickly as possible.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<h3 id=\"chair-of-ispa-steve-leighton-said\">Chair of ISPA, Steve Leighton said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>We welcome the Government’s announcement of a dispensation from building control regulations for installing gigabit-capable broadband in flats and houses, which will let our members accelerate much-needed infrastructure upgrades and support government’s target of nationwide gigabit-capable broadband by 2032.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">We remain fully committed to building safety and will keep working with Government, members and regulators to ensure the final dispensation gives clear guidance so broadband can be installed safely and efficiently.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Added stakeholder quote ","public_timestamp":"2026-07-09T14:57:28Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-09T11:01:00Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ece1fd0da7b592375/s216_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9eab418ab055592384/s300_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9e49b9c0597fdafac5/s465_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ea3c2a28abb50cd89/s630_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9e0808eaf43b50cd86/s712_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ea3c2a28abb50cd88/s960_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"press_release","first_published_at":"2026-07-09T12:01:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/expanded-support-for-residents-living-with-unsafe-cladding","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/expanded-support-for-residents-living-with-unsafe-cladding","base_path":"/government/news/expanded-support-for-residents-living-with-unsafe-cladding","content_id":"2b61f398-058d-4d7e-8f57-8a793d6a2001","document_type":"press_release","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-09T14:57:28Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Expanded support for residents living with unsafe cladding","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/expanded-support-for-residents-living-with-unsafe-cladding","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1419","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","content_id":"1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649","details":{"acronym":"MHCLG","brand":"ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ea3c2a28abb50cd88/s960_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9eab418ab055592384/s300_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Ministry of Housing,<br/>Communities &amp; <br/>Local Government"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1419","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","content_id":"1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649","details":{"acronym":"MHCLG","brand":"ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ea3c2a28abb50cd88/s960_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9eab418ab055592384/s300_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Ministry of Housing,<br/>Communities &amp; <br/>Local Government"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/rachel-blake","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/rachel-blake","base_path":"/government/people/rachel-blake","content_id":"5fe382f9-0688-4a37-ac84-4097dd71e6c3","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-22T08:45:32Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Rachel Blake MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/rachel-blake","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/samantha-dixon","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/samantha-dixon","base_path":"/government/people/samantha-dixon","content_id":"2f60a86b-1ccd-49e7-b991-5517e4c9bbe3","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-23T08:17:59Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Samantha Dixon MBE MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/samantha-dixon","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1419","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","content_id":"1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649","details":{"acronym":"MHCLG","brand":"ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9ea3c2a28abb50cd88/s960_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668f9d9eab418ab055592384/s300_2_Marsham_Street_1_-_960x640.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Ministry of Housing,<br/>Communities &amp; <br/>Local Government"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-housing-communities-local-government","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/economic-secretary-to-the-treasury--3","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/economic-secretary-to-the-treasury--3","base_path":"/government/ministers/economic-secretary-to-the-treasury--3","content_id":"60e177b0-be7e-4b6b-a0e8-8291952cefa8","details":{"body":"<p>The Economic Secretary to the Treasury (EST) is the City Minister and is responsible for financial services policy, reform and regulation. She is also responsible for some specific elements of tax policy. EST also supports the Chancellor on multilateral international policy and engagement.  </p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <p>Specific financial services responsibilities include: </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Engagement with the financial services sector </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Financial conduct and financial stability, including relationships with the FCA and PRA </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Competitiveness and growth of the financial services sector </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Banking and consumer credit </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Insurance and pensions markets </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Financial inclusion and capability </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Sustainable finance </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Fintech, digitalisation and cryptoassets </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>International financial services policy </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Cash and Payments including Royal Mint </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Elements of tax policy including financial services tax, ISAs and savings tax  </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Financial sanctions and countering economic crime, including the Office for Financial Sanctions Implementation (OFSI) </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Supporting the Chancellor on international policy work, including: </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Multilateral development banks </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Ukraine –  financing, sanctions, economic pressure  </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>G20 presidency planning </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Trade </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Women in Finance, Women in the economy and the gender pay gap  </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>The Treasury’s interest in Overseas Territories and Crown Dependencies issues</p>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-08-14T17:16:20Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Economic Secretary to the Treasury","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/economic-secretary-to-the-treasury--3","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--289","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--289","base_path":"/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--289","content_id":"a7b372be-2476-4a22-a87c-aca0513831a2","details":{"body":"<ul>\n  <li>Building safety, regulations, Building Safety Regulator and remediation </li>\n  <li>Net Zero and energy efficiency </li>\n  <li>Grenfell Inquiry response </li>\n  <li>Grenfell Community, Tower and Memorial </li>\n  <li>Fire policy and operations </li>\n  <li>Resilience, recovery, and emergencies </li>\n  <li>Elections policy  </li>\n  <li>Planning casework </li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-09-15T09:40:54Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Parliamentary Under-Secretary of State (Minister for Building Safety, Fire and Democracy)","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--289","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/housing-local-and-community/housing-and-communities","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/housing-local-and-community/housing-and-communities","base_path":"/housing-local-and-community/housing-and-communities","content_id":"4ad66168-274d-4d83-9195-f4ab0ccc97cb","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Housing and communities (level 2)","notes_for_editors":"","url_override":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/housing-local-and-community","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/housing-local-and-community","base_path":"/housing-local-and-community","content_id":"4794066e-e3cc-425e-8cc4-e7ff3edb4c39","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Housing, local and community","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbdec2-0e62-4520-a7fd-6ffd5d36e03a","document_type":"homepage","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:00:23Z","schema_name":"homepage","title":"GOV.UK homepage","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-16T20:32:02Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Housing, local and community","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/housing-local-and-community","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2022-02-14T14:24:18Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Housing and communities","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/housing-local-and-community/housing-and-communities","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/housing-local-and-community/planning-and-building","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/housing-local-and-community/planning-and-building","base_path":"/housing-local-and-community/planning-and-building","content_id":"e3147d4f-4bd5-4a14-a386-4ba7ccb058b4","details":{"internal_name":"Planning and building (merged, level 2)","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/housing-local-and-community","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/housing-local-and-community","base_path":"/housing-local-and-community","content_id":"4794066e-e3cc-425e-8cc4-e7ff3edb4c39","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Housing, local and community","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbdec2-0e62-4520-a7fd-6ffd5d36e03a","document_type":"homepage","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:00:23Z","schema_name":"homepage","title":"GOV.UK homepage","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-16T20:32:02Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Housing, local and community","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/housing-local-and-community","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-08-24T11:05:58Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Planning and building","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/housing-local-and-community/planning-and-building","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2026-07-09T15:57:28+01:00","publishing_app":"whitehall","publishing_request_id":"22-1783609048.712-10.13.22.18-2356","publishing_scheduled_at":null,"rendering_app":"frontend","scheduled_publishing_delay_seconds":null,"schema_name":"news_article","title":"Expanded support for residents living with unsafe cladding","updated_at":"2026-09-10T10:49:55+01:00","withdrawn_notice":{}}